{"kind":"request","text":"CLI under load: sessions, verify and three defects. Child of the load findings a6847815 (items 2 and 3) and the launchd and HTTPS findings e6a5cd22 (items 5 and 6).\n\n1. Session reuse. Under load one key made 1,077 session requests in a run and hit REQUESTS_PER_KEY (64, packages/scope/src/sessions.ts:385). The cap stays. The CLI keeps the issued session (token, membership, key, reads, ends) in the DAP_HOME private store and reuses it until 30 seconds before `ends`; a session refused expired or unauthorized is discarded and one new request made. Witness: 1,000 reads in one minute by one key make at most three session requests.\n2. Refusal words. A 429 on a session request is reported `rate-limited` with the window, never `forbidden`; the signed-read fallback (packages/cli/src/commands.ts:121, 125, 722, 723) runs only on `forbidden`. `dap verify --all` never reports \"incomplete\" because of a session limit: it reports the limit.\n3. `dap verify --all` pages every scope of the room under a byte and time budget with progress lines and an explicit stopped-at outcome, instead of the fixed 64 scopes (a room with an inbox per member passes 64 at about 60 members; 585 s to report the limit at 578 members). The register's entries that the room's claim chain names are read through the room's membership session (chained reads, sessions.ts:314), not the signed window, so a room other than the register's first verifies the register.\n4. Founding after the window: the evaluation found the same key cannot create another room once its last register signature is no longer recent. Find the cause (a pre-read of the register summary is the suspect). Founding on an `open` register must not depend on the key having signed before. Fix it in this head, or report the rule that intends it.\n5. `dap act set-role --target @m1` crashes with a CanonicalError (NaN target): a handle target is resolved as elsewhere or refused with a message.\n6. The \"outcome unknown\" answer (first issueInvitation in the validation) is the honest answer when the acknowledgment times out; the message says the act may still take effect and how to continue (the validation continued after 2 s and found it verified).\n\nOne gate, exact-head review, PD-2 note with the witness numbers. Order: after the LAN keys slice.","body":{"conditions":"Items 1 to 6 built or item 4 reported with the rule; witness numbers in a PD-2 note; one gate; exact-head checker approval; landed on main.","target_head":"ca7b16bc9a297912a065ca97773b510f6f14dcdc","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}